    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch10-21: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.32";
    dc:description "Specific compact cognitive architectures can be benchmarked, but their success would not show that they capture the unique core of human thinking. The claim lacks a discriminating consequence against more complex or implementation-dependent accounts.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/none";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Without quantitative definitions of the cognitive core, independence from neural details, rule simplicity, and what would count as fundamentally special, behavioral equivalence cannot confirm or refute the statement.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Core and simplicity are undefined.", "Multiple implementations can fit the same behavior.", "The claim combines empirical and metaphysical assertions.";
